<item><title>Tambura clashes displace 300 households to camps and nearby communities</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/ss/tambura-clashes-displace-300-households-to-camps-and-nearby-02bb1f/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/ss/tambura-clashes-displace-300-households-to-camps-and-nearby-02bb1f/</guid><category>South Sudan</category><description>Officials report 100 households in Maboiku and 200 in Sinawiri as South Sudan&apos;s government plans an assessment of those who fled.</description><pubDate>Thu, 19 Nov 2026 08:49:10 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/ss.jpg" length="35634" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/ss.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
